b15f5a2d2.png)\n\nNow, since the vector field $F=3\\,i$ is parallel to ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{4},$ there is zero net flow through these two sides. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nSo, our expression for the flux reduces to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNow, since the vector field is uniform, the net outflow through ${C}_{1}$ will cancel with the net inflow through ${C}_{3}.$ That is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s=-{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s\\,⟹\\,{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186540276 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186179646.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186540276 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "2559158e-ccf7-5367-8a90-3d49434ee990" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186542277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1045 "Conditional Variance for Discrete Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186542277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186541422 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "dc48a99d-604a-5b95-8182-825cd7371ab2" #edb/ref 17592186045417